  "titulo": "Future perfect: regular verbs",
  "subtitulo": "Habré terminado, habrás comido, habrán vivido.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Future perfect = haber in the future (habré, habrás, habrá, habremos, habrán) + past participle (-ado / -ido): habré terminado = I will have finished. Nothing goes between habré and the participle.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "habré / habrás / habrá / habremos / habrán",
            "+ participle"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "haber (future)"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "habré"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "habrás"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "habrá"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "habremos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "habrán"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Regular participles: **-ar → -ado** (**hablado**), **-er / -ir → -ido** (**comido, vivido**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The participle **never changes** here, and nothing goes between **habré** and it. Pronouns and **no** go in front: **ya lo habré terminado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Uses: something done before a future point (**para el lunes habré terminado**) and guesses about the past (**habrá salido**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: future of **haber** + **-ado / -ido**."
        }
      ]
    },
